PART 3 — Block diagram, section A: open the port
Everything in this section goes at the far left of the diagram, before any loop.
3.1 Place three VIs, left to right
1.	Functions » Instrument I/O » Serial » VISA Configure Serial Port
2.	Functions » Instrument I/O » Serial » VISA Set I/O Buffer Size
3.	Functions » Instrument I/O » Serial » VISA Flush I/O Buffer
3.2 Wire the chain
•	VISA Resource terminal → VISA resource name input of Configure
•	Configure's VISA resource name out → Set Buffer Size's resource in
•	Set Buffer Size out → Flush's resource in
•	Chain the error out → error in wires the same way, left to right
3.3 Create the constants
For each input below: right-click the input terminal → Create » Constant, then type the value.
VISA Configure Serial Port:
Input	Value	Note
baud rate	921600	
data bits	8	
parity	0	No parity
stop bits	10	10 means one stop bit
flow control	0	None
timeout	1000	milliseconds
enable termination char	FALSE	right-click the constant to toggle it
If you change nothing else on this page, change the termination character. LabVIEW defaults it to TRUE with 0x0A, and your binary payloads are full of 0x0A bytes. Leave it on and your reads will chop messages in half at random.
VISA Set I/O Buffer Size: mask 16, size 65536
VISA Flush I/O Buffer: mask 16
